i'll agree with this one. we're using this at work to back up a set
of approx 10 servers and it is rather nice (once you get your head
round how it works). lovely to see way it reschedules full dumps and
promotes/demotes dumps to differing dump levels to try balance out
the total backup size.

if you're going to use amanda, make sure to get the
CVS code, amanda-242-branch for the stable stuff, or HEAD for new
2.5.0 code.

only niggly thing about amanda: it won't append to a tape.

--paulj

On Tue, 31 Oct 2000, Mike Tibor wrote:

> I've never used Arkeia, but you might also want to look at Amanda. Amanda
> is a pretty comprehensive network backup package that uses either gnu tar
> or whatever version of dump that's on the machine you're backing up.
