> ...Any ideas about why this error occurs?
> 
> f77 -O4  \
>         -o dimension dimension.f epsprg.o
> param.h: In program `dimension':
> In file included from dimension.f:39:
> param.h:26:
>            parameter (nbound=max(nbins,ndatar))
>                              ^
> Invalid declaration of or reference to symbol `max' at (^) [initially seen
> at (^)]
> make: *** [dimension] Error 1
  max is a macro defined in a system include file.
  the error can be fixed by adding 'include <file-name.h>' to
dimension.f,
  where file-name is the name of the file containing the
definition of map().
  to find the file, you could try:
     grep -w map /usr/include/*.h
     grep -w map /usr/include/*/*.h, etc

  good luck,
