With regards to your message at 03:02 PM 11/1/00, Tom Heibel. Where you stated:
>I need a driver for the Diamond SupraMax 56k PCI modem.  I'm running 
>Redhat 7.0.  I would be happy to try a legacy driver if someone has it.
>
>Thanks for your help.
>
>Respectfully,
>Tom Heibel
>Aspen Systems, Inc.



It's a WinModem Tom.
I doubt you will have much luck  with it!

http://www.idir.net/~gromitkc/20001025a.html

There has been some progress with making it a "LinModem" , but so far only 
a binary module for X86 kernels of the 2.2.14 vintage have been 
released.  Company doing it is called Olitec, and if you read French you 
may find out more at:
http://www.olitec.com/pci56kv2.html

The Olitec is another implementation of the same Conexant (Rockwell) chip.
If source gets released perhaps someone will port it for Alpha, but doing 
this is not for the faint of heart..

If you have an ISA slot on the motherboard I would recommend looking at 
some of the 3COM/USR ISA modems still available. They are true modems, and 
have jumpers too..
The 5687 is my favourite.

Good luck!


