Maurice,

Thanks for the help.  This is an issue we all need to overcome if we are =
going to use PCI modems in any Linux box because the motherboards being =
produced today have no ISA slots at all.

Thanks again.
Tom
  ----- Original Message -----=20
  From: Maurice Hilarius=20
  To: axp-list@redhat.com=20
  Sent: Wednesday, November 01, 2000 5:35 PM
  Subject: Re: Linux Driver


  With regards to your message at 03:02 PM 11/1/00, Tom Heibel. Where =
you stated:

    I need a driver for the Diamond SupraMax 56k PCI modem.  I'm running =
Redhat 7.0.  I would be happy to try a legacy driver if someone has it.
    =20
    Thanks for your help.
    =20
    Respectfully,
    Tom Heibel
    Aspen Systems, Inc.



  It's a WinModem Tom.
  I doubt you will have much luck  with it!

  http://www.idir.net/~gromitkc/20001025a.html

  There has been some progress with making it a "LinModem" , but so far =
only a binary module for X86 kernels of the 2.2.14 vintage have been =
released.  Company doing it is called Olitec, and if you read French you =
may find out more at:
  http://www.olitec.com/pci56kv2.html

  The Olitec is another implementation of the same Conexant (Rockwell) =
chip.
  If source gets released perhaps someone will port it for Alpha, but =
doing this is not for the faint of heart..

  If you have an ISA slot on the motherboard I would recommend looking =
at some of the 3COM/USR ISA modems still available. They are true =
modems, and have jumpers too..
  The 5687 is my favourite.

  Good luck!



  With our best regards,


