On Thu, Nov 16, 2000 at 10:22:55AM -0500, Jay Estabrook wrote:
> On Thu, Nov 16, 2000 at 08:49:51AM +0100, Helge Kreutzmann wrote:
> > 
> > >>>AllocOSMIOB failed
> > 
> 
> That message, "AllocOSMIOB failed", comes from the Adaptec driver, and
> indicates that, for some reason, it failed to alloc a new IOB from its
> free list.
> 
> So, yes, it seems to related to SCSI, and no, I have no idea what you
> should do... :-\
> 
> Good luck.
> 
> --Jay++

Thanks. Removing the offending harddisk from the SCSI chain solved the
problem, I can now boot again. Do you know where I can find out about
this IOB ? Because I would be interested if my adaptec (or the cable maybe)
has the problem of driving more than disk or if I simply bought a broken
hard drive.

Thanks again

