With regards to your message at 08:03 AM 11/19/00, Richard June. Where you 
stated:
><<<Snip>>>

>The PICMG stuff doesn't allow for hot swap, but CompacPCI does, we use
>that as well.
>Our backplane allows for two SBCs and you could probably fit some of the
>dual x86 SBCs there w/out a problem, so you've got 4 procs and 10 PCI
>slots there, I'm not sure about the Alpha stuff though, that card was
>the first Alpha SBC I've ever seen, who actually sells those things?
>Compaq's website doesn't seem to mention them.
Compaq sold the last part of the OEM group last year.
If you go to one of the older Digital Semiconductor pages you can find it. 
However, after a moment a redirector will take you to a "page not found" 
message.
It IS there, but only for a moment!

For example:
http://www.digital.com/semiconductor/

Compaq is now in the "denial we ever had a Digital OEM division" stage..


