Thanks for the quick response.  It's a shame Veritas doesn't include the
source for the RH x86 client, since it "should" compile OK on AXP just as
well (it's essentially doing a network copy)....

I have my Alpha, a Multia VX40, dedicated for mail only.  It, along with
my Pentium Multias, are all crammed into a small spot (I'm in a small
apartment), and I don't have any external SCSI stuff to mess with.  The
SCSI tape drive is internal and physically in my NT Server.  I also own
BackupExec for NT.

This is getting crazy....

Maybe I can do something like this for backup:
1. create cron job (run as root?) to run a shell script
2. shell script to tar/gzip everything to a FTP site or HTTP site
   (no SAMBA or NFS stuph is installed on the Multia)
3. NT BackupExec gets the .tar.gz to tape
I really have no idea how to get .2. running.  Does anyone have any
thoughts?  I've never tar'd anything over the network...

Maybe I can do something like this for restore:
1. Pick out the files thru the NT BackupExec GUI
2. Restore the files to a FTP site
3. Let the AXP box grab the files and replace them
I am afraid that the typing on the Linux files will get clobbered when
they are sitting on an NT box before they get to the Multia.  Any thoughts
on that issue?


Thanks!



