Dear all,
   I have RH 6.2 AXP on XP1000 machine. I tested hard disk performance
with hdparm. The result (checked several times) looks strange to me

# /sbin/hdparm -gt /dev/sda5

/dev/sda5:
 geometry     = 1106/255/63, sectors = 9703260, start = 8064630
 Timing buffered disk reads:  64 MB in  3.93 seconds = 16.29 MB/sec

I do have UW SCSI hard drive and a controller (below), and would expect
preformance closer to 40 MB/sec or at least something over 20MB/sec to
be sure it works not just in fast SCSI mode.

I am new to Linux, so maybe I'm just missing something here. Could you
point out what is wrong here, or is it normal?
Thanks!
--Zufar


